From 068bba47a299432784afafa6c6a421a14f54c726 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Huy Le <levanhuy96@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 10:11:53 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] 10226: Demangler analyzer: don't demangle the same mangled name twice

Since GP-3040, AbstractDemanglerAnalyzer.demangleSymbols also demangles
non-primary symbols at each address after demangling the primary symbol.
Applying the demangled name renames the primary function symbol and
leaves the mangled name behind as a non-primary symbol (SetLabelPrimaryCmd
re-creates it), so the same mangled name was demangled and applied a
second time. DemangledFunction.isAlreadyDemangled does not stop the
second apply (the signature source it just set is ANALYSIS or lower), and
isParameterMismatch then bookmarks 'Couldn't apply demangled signature -
mismatch with existing signature' at every function whose mangled name
carries a return type and parameters (C++ templates, Swift functions).
The primary symbol iterator may also revisit an address after the symbol
changes, re-running the non-primary pass.

Track the addresses processed by demangleSymbols so an address is only
processed once, and skip the non-primary symbol whose name is the mangled
name that the primary pass just demangled. Other mangled names at the
same address are still demangled, preserving GP-3040's intent.

Fixes #10212
